[[:db/retract 17592186120156 :question/answer-fields 17592186117142] {:db/id 17592186119947 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-449eabe4-56aa-5632-8405-aab3edd3f407" "question-e89f4c3b-6723-58b1-b21d-dbb9b8ced775" "question-de097a4f-c54e-5f8e-b869-e4dc2af58fad"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119949 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0b5962d7-05b0-532b-8c6d-f094e8fba0fc" "question-2ed8ed9c-cb01-554d-a0b3-14bce9a90d30" "question-4d730355-3ecf-557f-807f-e7e1ed97b6ff"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119948 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1b9a8797-8d36-57ec-bbd4-59c107c7ab69" "question-076128a8-7495-5bb6-b7b4-2c35cb671771" "question-7326acab-616b-5037-877a-7e6bd9629162"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-449eabe4-56aa-5632-8405-aab3edd3f407" :question/id #uuid "449eabe4-56aa-5632-8405-aab3edd3f407" :question/math-academy-id "q-131973" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{3}t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3}⟩$ for $t\\ge 0,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(0,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,0,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,0,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\sqrt{3}t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3}⟩ & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}t=0 \\\\ {t}^{2}=0 \\\\ {t}^{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=0.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,2t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\sqrt{3},\\,2(0),\\,3({0}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{3},0,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3+0+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-af4cee66-027d-5ab7-8663-bfb226292ce7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-af4cee66-027d-5ab7-8663-bfb226292ce7" :answer-field/id #uuid "af4cee66-027d-5ab7-8663-bfb226292ce7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6192c0d5-ad72-575b-8a2f-1a7e46fd57a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6d75b37-7ea1-5e02-b969-0619510bbb86" "answer-b474040b-15fe-5f81-9135-6af3cb2ab312" "answer-ca8f7d86-99fe-52e7-8a9e-f1de3df11de1" "answer-b8777a7b-55af-5c7c-909e-036d3340c2bc" "answer-6192c0d5-ad72-575b-8a2f-1a7e46fd57a5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6d75b37-7ea1-5e02-b969-0619510bbb86" :answer/id #uuid "c6d75b37-7ea1-5e02-b969-0619510bbb86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b474040b-15fe-5f81-9135-6af3cb2ab312" :answer/id #uuid "b474040b-15fe-5f81-9135-6af3cb2ab312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca8f7d86-99fe-52e7-8a9e-f1de3df11de1" :answer/id #uuid "ca8f7d86-99fe-52e7-8a9e-f1de3df11de1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8777a7b-55af-5c7c-909e-036d3340c2bc" :answer/id #uuid "b8777a7b-55af-5c7c-909e-036d3340c2bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6192c0d5-ad72-575b-8a2f-1a7e46fd57a5" :answer/id #uuid "6192c0d5-ad72-575b-8a2f-1a7e46fd57a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e89f4c3b-6723-58b1-b21d-dbb9b8ced775" :question/id #uuid "e89f4c3b-6723-58b1-b21d-dbb9b8ced775" :question/math-academy-id "q-83404" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3},{t}^{2},\\,\\,t⟩$ for $t>0$, use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(\\frac{2}{3},1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(\\frac{2}{3},1,1)$ on the given curve. We know that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},1,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3},{t}^{2},\\,\\,t⟩ & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ t=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(\\frac{2}{3},1,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(1),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{t}^{2},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t,\\,2,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(1) & =⟨4,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-2i+4j-4k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(1){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{3}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1859a39-a2db-5a73-b35c-f7fe6ddee607"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1859a39-a2db-5a73-b35c-f7fe6ddee607" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1859a39-a2db-5a73-b35c-f7fe6ddee607" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1b297cdb-aecf-5f48-af66-84c29ddda497" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b1a80722-6c7c-5c77-acb3-2b2fa7e23bbb" "answer-1b297cdb-aecf-5f48-af66-84c29ddda497" "answer-123d29d6-8aaf-5afb-862b-e46ce76281e2" "answer-2f0e8910-4151-5310-9c16-3f2d1d8be9a0" "answer-2bc57f81-b019-581e-9c4a-3f95a1c41bbd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1a80722-6c7c-5c77-acb3-2b2fa7e23bbb" :answer/id #uuid "b1a80722-6c7c-5c77-acb3-2b2fa7e23bbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b297cdb-aecf-5f48-af66-84c29ddda497" :answer/id #uuid "1b297cdb-aecf-5f48-af66-84c29ddda497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-123d29d6-8aaf-5afb-862b-e46ce76281e2" :answer/id #uuid "123d29d6-8aaf-5afb-862b-e46ce76281e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f0e8910-4151-5310-9c16-3f2d1d8be9a0" :answer/id #uuid "2f0e8910-4151-5310-9c16-3f2d1d8be9a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bc57f81-b019-581e-9c4a-3f95a1c41bbd" :answer/id #uuid "2bc57f81-b019-581e-9c4a-3f95a1c41bbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351507 :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩ & =⟨2,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(2,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(1),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(1) & =⟨0,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-4i+2j+4k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+16} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)\\times {r}^{″}(1)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(1){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{3}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-de097a4f-c54e-5f8e-b869-e4dc2af58fad" :question/id #uuid "de097a4f-c54e-5f8e-b869-e4dc2af58fad" :question/math-academy-id "q-83407" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{2t},\\,2t⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to compute the curvature at the point $P(1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,1,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{2t},\\,2t⟩ & =⟨1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}=1 \\\\ {e}^{2t}=1 \\\\ 2t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=0.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(1,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,2{e}^{2t},\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,2,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{2t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,4{e}^{2t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨1,4,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-8i+2j+2k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{{3}^{3}}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-998024b6-f7ae-51f5-8648-5d3da46e7c95"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-998024b6-f7ae-51f5-8648-5d3da46e7c95" :answer-field/id #uuid "998024b6-f7ae-51f5-8648-5d3da46e7c95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-77770b63-6e34-588d-bcf9-716fc7c40db7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77770b63-6e34-588d-bcf9-716fc7c40db7" "answer-33ab4b89-4470-5e8b-aee7-5a0fe5da5f2f" "answer-54fa053c-1b85-5eca-ba73-3ffa7456b013" "answer-fc8a20ec-0cfe-5f28-9075-f6395f297291" "answer-26a6f877-facd-5ea0-8579-e0d7c191bd3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77770b63-6e34-588d-bcf9-716fc7c40db7" :answer/id #uuid "77770b63-6e34-588d-bcf9-716fc7c40db7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33ab4b89-4470-5e8b-aee7-5a0fe5da5f2f" :answer/id #uuid "33ab4b89-4470-5e8b-aee7-5a0fe5da5f2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54fa053c-1b85-5eca-ba73-3ffa7456b013" :answer/id #uuid "54fa053c-1b85-5eca-ba73-3ffa7456b013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc8a20ec-0cfe-5f28-9075-f6395f297291" :answer/id #uuid "fc8a20ec-0cfe-5f28-9075-f6395f297291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26a6f877-facd-5ea0-8579-e0d7c191bd3a" :answer/id #uuid "26a6f877-facd-5ea0-8579-e0d7c191bd3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186266124 :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(0,-3,4\\pi )$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨0,-3,4\\pi ⟩ \\\\ ⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4t⟩ & =⟨0,-3,4\\pi ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-3 \\\\ 4t=4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, $t=\\pi .$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(0,-3,4\\pi )$ is at the tip of $r(\\pi ).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$  and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,4⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${r}^{″}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross-product and its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-12i-9k \\\\  & =3(-4i-3k) \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =3\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =3(5) \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{{5}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-0b5962d7-05b0-532b-8c6d-f094e8fba0fc" :question/id #uuid "0b5962d7-05b0-532b-8c6d-f094e8fba0fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-165246" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨6t,\\,{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$ \n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that* ${r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=18(-{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+2t\\,k).$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\  & =3⟨2,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =3\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{({t}^{2})}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{4+{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =3({t}^{2}+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $({t}^{2}+2)>0$ for any real value $t.$\n\nSince we are told that\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=18(-{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+2t\\,k),\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =18\\sqrt{{(-{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(-2)}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =18\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+4+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =18\\sqrt{{({t}^{2}+2)}^{2}} \\\\  & =18({t}^{2}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18({t}^{2}+2)}{{(3({t}^{2}+2))}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3{({t}^{2}+2)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bb12e737-fb94-52b4-acc6-88a1547c5cff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bb12e737-fb94-52b4-acc6-88a1547c5cff" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb12e737-fb94-52b4-acc6-88a1547c5cff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dadaec8e-26a0-5da2-84a3-c4a2326b68ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f3e2e194-e553-5ed9-8cc4-61ffcab44e2a" "answer-a2bacd0f-24fc-559e-9299-4608d1542763" "answer-a36ef49d-80e1-577c-8d08-f4a49353a82d" "answer-dadaec8e-26a0-5da2-84a3-c4a2326b68ba" "answer-ebf3cf16-f0ca-5637-9809-9b6a71caec58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3e2e194-e553-5ed9-8cc4-61ffcab44e2a" :answer/id #uuid "f3e2e194-e553-5ed9-8cc4-61ffcab44e2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6({t}^{2}+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2bacd0f-24fc-559e-9299-4608d1542763" :answer/id #uuid "a2bacd0f-24fc-559e-9299-4608d1542763" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{({t}^{2}+2)}^{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a36ef49d-80e1-577c-8d08-f4a49353a82d" :answer/id #uuid "a36ef49d-80e1-577c-8d08-f4a49353a82d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3({t}^{2}+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dadaec8e-26a0-5da2-84a3-c4a2326b68ba" :answer/id #uuid "dadaec8e-26a0-5da2-84a3-c4a2326b68ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3{({t}^{2}+2)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ebf3cf16-f0ca-5637-9809-9b6a71caec58" :answer/id #uuid "ebf3cf16-f0ca-5637-9809-9b6a71caec58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{({t}^{2}+2)}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ed8ed9c-cb01-554d-a0b3-14bce9a90d30" :question/id #uuid "2ed8ed9c-cb01-554d-a0b3-14bce9a90d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-86796" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨6-3{t}^{2},\\,4,\\,6t-2⟩$, use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-3{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-2)⟩=⟨-6t,\\,0,\\,6⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-6t)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36({t}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the second derivative ${r}^{″}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6)⟩=⟨-6,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the cross-product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨-6t,0,6⟩\\times ⟨-6,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -6t & 0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-6t & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-6t & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-36\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the magnitude of the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{36}{{(6\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1})}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{6({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d4649305-d5dc-5854-97b6-ea90ae323c38"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d4649305-d5dc-5854-97b6-ea90ae323c38" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4649305-d5dc-5854-97b6-ea90ae323c38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-823f8f03-83d5-50e3-94a5-43fd37ec5943" :answer-field/choices ["answer-823f8f03-83d5-50e3-94a5-43fd37ec5943" "answer-7b7fddc5-e9f3-50c7-becb-6d8967a0296e" "answer-c975a084-8904-518b-9668-d1ed45bc4672" "answer-0d5c28aa-e40b-5d7d-9621-b891be1115bb" "answer-fc0a86bb-661c-5cb1-b20b-55887d482bef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-823f8f03-83d5-50e3-94a5-43fd37ec5943" :answer/id #uuid "823f8f03-83d5-50e3-94a5-43fd37ec5943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7b7fddc5-e9f3-50c7-becb-6d8967a0296e" :answer/id #uuid "7b7fddc5-e9f3-50c7-becb-6d8967a0296e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c975a084-8904-518b-9668-d1ed45bc4672" :answer/id #uuid "c975a084-8904-518b-9668-d1ed45bc4672" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{(36{t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d5c28aa-e40b-5d7d-9621-b891be1115bb" :answer/id #uuid "0d5c28aa-e40b-5d7d-9621-b891be1115bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{({t}^{2}+1)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc0a86bb-661c-5cb1-b20b-55887d482bef" :answer/id #uuid "fc0a86bb-661c-5cb1-b20b-55887d482bef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d730355-3ecf-557f-807f-e7e1ed97b6ff" :question/id #uuid "4d730355-3ecf-557f-807f-e7e1ed97b6ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-165241" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,t-2⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$ \n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+4k.$*" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are told that\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+4k,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2840ac15-6a7c-5a69-ab78-2aa96a22daa0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2840ac15-6a7c-5a69-ab78-2aa96a22daa0" :answer-field/id #uuid "2840ac15-6a7c-5a69-ab78-2aa96a22daa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2c36339d-550d-50a9-ac87-d1b79dc3d514" :answer-field/choices ["answer-588ff593-33c8-57cf-b908-2d3cd4e4eda4" "answer-911da293-aa1c-5630-aa8e-6b4e6f105496" "answer-2c36339d-550d-50a9-ac87-d1b79dc3d514" "answer-00c78679-4fdc-52dc-a8e7-46e00dcb62f0" "answer-4a238725-2bd1-54ac-bbb6-7159963ecd45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-588ff593-33c8-57cf-b908-2d3cd4e4eda4" :answer/id #uuid "588ff593-33c8-57cf-b908-2d3cd4e4eda4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-911da293-aa1c-5630-aa8e-6b4e6f105496" :answer/id #uuid "911da293-aa1c-5630-aa8e-6b4e6f105496" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c36339d-550d-50a9-ac87-d1b79dc3d514" :answer/id #uuid "2c36339d-550d-50a9-ac87-d1b79dc3d514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00c78679-4fdc-52dc-a8e7-46e00dcb62f0" :answer/id #uuid "00c78679-4fdc-52dc-a8e7-46e00dcb62f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a238725-2bd1-54ac-bbb6-7159963ecd45" :answer/id #uuid "4a238725-2bd1-54ac-bbb6-7159963ecd45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{20}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1b9a8797-8d36-57ec-bbd4-59c107c7ab69" :question/id #uuid "1b9a8797-8d36-57ec-bbd4-59c107c7ab69" :question/math-academy-id "q-64755" :question/problem "Find the curvature of the curve $r(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$, as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩=⟨8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}}=\\sqrt{100{cos}^{2}⁡2t}=10|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),-6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩=⟨-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,0⟩\\times ⟨-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & 0 \\\\ -16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ -16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & 12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =(96\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-96\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}=\\frac{0}{(10|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t|)^{3}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3bb55b1d-75c9-5fb5-9c67-287204de1c0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3bb55b1d-75c9-5fb5-9c67-287204de1c0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bb55b1d-75c9-5fb5-9c67-287204de1c0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c1a067a-8d2b-5397-8bd3-24d1405573aa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6c1a067a-8d2b-5397-8bd3-24d1405573aa" "answer-cf174ac9-d620-53ea-82b8-3479aa692564" "answer-734228d6-96a3-5705-9452-b117125fb933" "answer-a00913e3-150c-5757-bc29-0491a7b33dc4" "answer-1ce26e03-d563-568e-aa5d-992e2c4b26f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c1a067a-8d2b-5397-8bd3-24d1405573aa" :answer/id #uuid "6c1a067a-8d2b-5397-8bd3-24d1405573aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf174ac9-d620-53ea-82b8-3479aa692564" :answer/id #uuid "cf174ac9-d620-53ea-82b8-3479aa692564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-734228d6-96a3-5705-9452-b117125fb933" :answer/id #uuid "734228d6-96a3-5705-9452-b117125fb933" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a00913e3-150c-5757-bc29-0491a7b33dc4" :answer/id #uuid "a00913e3-150c-5757-bc29-0491a7b33dc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1\\,000|\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t{|}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ce26e03-d563-568e-aa5d-992e2c4b26f4" :answer/id #uuid "1ce26e03-d563-568e-aa5d-992e2c4b26f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1\\,000|\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t{|}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-076128a8-7495-5bb6-b7b4-2c35cb671771" :question/id #uuid "076128a8-7495-5bb6-b7b4-2c35cb671771" :question/math-academy-id "q-132071" :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨t,\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩$ as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4t+1}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4t+1}}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} &  \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}})}{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{4t+1}}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{(4t+1)^{3}}}{8\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(4t+1)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-afb164f4-0f92-5e1b-9127-b2a957f405bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-afb164f4-0f92-5e1b-9127-b2a957f405bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "afb164f4-0f92-5e1b-9127-b2a957f405bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ac65a6f7-9738-5d33-887a-9ad58c1f5490" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f2e3162a-cf34-5775-9fc4-941bbc74028c" "answer-0917bfa0-bfa9-5b16-886f-9cc52438c52b" "answer-602841f2-5541-552b-907f-100fdf2ade39" "answer-ac65a6f7-9738-5d33-887a-9ad58c1f5490" "answer-499f4d91-d45c-54cb-8843-70596b66dfbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2e3162a-cf34-5775-9fc4-941bbc74028c" :answer/id #uuid "f2e3162a-cf34-5775-9fc4-941bbc74028c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{(4t+1)^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0917bfa0-bfa9-5b16-886f-9cc52438c52b" :answer/id #uuid "0917bfa0-bfa9-5b16-886f-9cc52438c52b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{4t+1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-602841f2-5541-552b-907f-100fdf2ade39" :answer/id #uuid "602841f2-5541-552b-907f-100fdf2ade39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{(4t+1)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac65a6f7-9738-5d33-887a-9ad58c1f5490" :answer/id #uuid "ac65a6f7-9738-5d33-887a-9ad58c1f5490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(4t+1)^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-499f4d91-d45c-54cb-8843-70596b66dfbb" :answer/id #uuid "499f4d91-d45c-54cb-8843-70596b66dfbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4\\sqrt{(4t+1)^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7326acab-616b-5037-877a-7e6bd9629162" :question/id #uuid "7326acab-616b-5037-877a-7e6bd9629162" :question/math-academy-id "q-34389" :question/problem "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ as a function of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2cos)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}}=\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩=⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0 \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =(-6{cos}^{2}⁡t-6{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-6\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t})^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(4{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t)^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9607fc20-f180-54be-8b8c-9a4822e7bd6e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9607fc20-f180-54be-8b8c-9a4822e7bd6e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9607fc20-f180-54be-8b8c-9a4822e7bd6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-24f0028a-7323-5cc0-87c2-f487c039cf16" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e44d4b63-0b17-5d85-b565-88b6b006fe00" "answer-ccc3fac5-5112-57d8-8ccd-d0b4ff66f35f" "answer-24f0028a-7323-5cc0-87c2-f487c039cf16" "answer-5c8f11ce-6526-5329-9795-0b707389fea2" "answer-027d08e5-4fb2-5cdf-8e69-94adcf33c27e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e44d4b63-0b17-5d85-b565-88b6b006fe00" :answer/id #uuid "e44d4b63-0b17-5d85-b565-88b6b006fe00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{(4{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccc3fac5-5112-57d8-8ccd-d0b4ff66f35f" :answer/id #uuid "ccc3fac5-5112-57d8-8ccd-d0b4ff66f35f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{(2{cos}^{2}⁡t+3{sin}^{2}⁡t)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24f0028a-7323-5cc0-87c2-f487c039cf16" :answer/id #uuid "24f0028a-7323-5cc0-87c2-f487c039cf16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{(4{cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c8f11ce-6526-5329-9795-0b707389fea2" :answer/id #uuid "5c8f11ce-6526-5329-9795-0b707389fea2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{(4{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-027d08e5-4fb2-5cdf-8e69-94adcf33c27e" :answer/id #uuid "027d08e5-4fb2-5cdf-8e69-94adcf33c27e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{({cos}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t)^{3/2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121136 :tutorial/content "Recall that if the curve $\\mathbf r(s)$ is parametrized by arc length $s,$ then the curvature of $\\mathbf{r}$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\kappa(s) =  \\left\\| \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}\\mathbf T}{\\textrm{d}s}  \\right\\|.\n$$\n\nMoreover, if $\\mathbf r(t)$ is parametrized by a general parameter $t,$ we have the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf T(t) = \\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|}$ is the unit tangent vector to the curve. \n\nIt can be shown that the curvature of $\\mathbf r(t)$ can also be found using the following cross product formula:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf r'(t) \\times \\mathbf r''(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^3}\n$$\n\nWe'll derive this formula at the end of the lesson. For now, let's get some practice at applying it." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121137 :tutorial/content "Suppose we have a plane curve $C$ that is parametrized by the vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\langle x(t), \\: y(t) \\rangle.\n$$\n\nAt first glance, it looks as though the cross product curvature formula cannot be applied since cross products apply to three-dimensional vectors, whereas the given vector $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ has only two dimensions.\n\nHowever, this curve can also be viewed as a curve in three-dimensional space that lies on the plane $z=0.$ In this case, $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ can be considered as a vector-valued function with $z$-component equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)= \\langle x(t), \\: y(t), \\: 0 \\rangle\n$$\n\nAs a result, the curvature $\\kappa$ of our plane curve $C$ can be calculated using our cross product formula:\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t)=\\dfrac{\\|{\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)}\\times {\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime\\prime}(t)}\\|}{\\|{\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)}\\|^3}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121138 :tutorial/content "Recall that if the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ is parametrized by a general parameter $t,$ then the curvature of $\\mathbf{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf T(t) = \\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|}$ is the unit tangent vector to the curve. \n\nHere, $\\mathbf r'(t)$ is a vector function and $\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|$ is a scalar function.\nSo, we differentiate $\\mathbf T(t)$ by using the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{∂}{∂t}(T) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖})\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)+\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}({r}^{′}(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖})\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)+\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\\cdot {r}^{″}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the cross product of a vector with itself equals $\\mathbf{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t)\\times {T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\\times (\\frac{∂}{∂t}(\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖})\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)+\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\\cdot {r}^{″}(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{2}}\\,({r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of both sides and use the fact that $\\mathbf T$ is a unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖T(t)\\times {T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{2}}\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ \\\\ ‖T(t)‖\\cdot ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{2}}\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ \\\\ 1\\cdot ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{2}}\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\kappa(t) = \\dfrac{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|} = \\dfrac{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\times \\mathbf r''(t) \\right\\|}{\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^3}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120035 :activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
